WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.729
The week before Commencement, Carlos gets a message by the trailer:

2
00:00:05.779 --> 00:00:11.898
Events needs his grounds crew on the main lawn Friday, all day, for the tent build.

3
00:00:11.948 --> 00:00:16.580
His crew is already booked solid, and it is not his call alone.

4
00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:24.234
This is job four, connect your team to the rest of Vanderbilt, and it is the job new managers do least,

5
00:00:24.284 --> 00:00:27.801
because nobody told them it was part of the job.

6
00:00:27.851 --> 00:00:33.895
Know the people: Carlos already knows the events coordinator by name, and his HCM,

7
00:00:33.945 --> 00:00:40.956
and the person in Finance who approves his overtime, because he met them before he needed them.

8
00:00:41.006 --> 00:00:47.941
Watch for what is coming: the Commencement schedule was on the grounds shop calendar in March,

9
00:00:47.991 --> 00:00:53.589
so his crew heard about the week from him, not from a message on a Thursday.

10
00:00:53.639 --> 00:01:00.427
Speak up for your team: at a picnic table with the printed schedule, Carlos shows the hours,

11
00:01:00.477 --> 00:01:08.379
names the conflict, and offers two options: the tent build Friday morning with the edging pushed to Monday,

12
00:01:08.429 --> 00:01:13.283
or the whole job Saturday with overtime. She picks Friday morning.

13
00:01:13.333 --> 00:01:20.938
Nobody worked the weekend. Commencement morning, the chairs are in rows and the crew steps back, proud.

14
00:01:20.988 --> 00:01:27.775
Your team needs things it does not control: approvals, information, help from other offices,

15
00:01:27.825 --> 00:01:31.194
and a fair hearing when someone asks too much.

16
00:01:31.244 --> 00:01:35.653
This week: have coffee with one person your team depends on.

